      "solution": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    h = list(map(int, data[1:1 + n]))\n    stack = []          # strictly decreasing heights\n    pairs = 0\n    for x in h:\n        while stack and stack[-1] < x:\n            pairs += 1  # the lower roof on the stack sees x\n            stack.pop()\n        if stack:\n            pairs += 1  # the roof on top of the stack sees x\n            if stack[-1] == x:\n                stack.pop()  # an equal roof hides everything behind it\n        stack.append(x)\n    print(pairs)\n\nmain()",
      "statement": "Every night the lamplighter of Lantern Street wonders how many pairs of roofs can see each other.\n\nThe street is a single row of [[N]] buildings. Two roofs <<see each other>> when every building standing between them is strictly lower than both of them. Two neighbouring roofs always see each other.\n\nCount the pairs of roofs that see each other.",
