    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Every night the lamplighter of Lantern Street wonders how many pairs of roofs can see each other.<br><br>The street is a single row of <var>N</var> buildings. Two roofs <strong>see each other</strong> when every building standing between them is strictly lower than both of them. Two neighbouring roofs always see each other.<br><br>Count the pairs of roofs that see each other.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1</strong>: an integer <var>N</var>, the number of buildings.<br><strong>Line 2</strong>: <var>N</var> space-separated integers <var>H</var>, the heights of the buildings from left to right.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>One integer</strong>: the number of pairs of roofs that see each other.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">2 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 100<br>1 &le; <var>H</var> &le; 100</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">6\n3 1 2 5 5 2</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">7</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
